The pedestrian street sign "Avenida Cero" is the decisive clue, as this is the famous car-free promenade in the historic center of Santa Cruz de la Sierra, Bolivia. Supporting evidence includes the Spanish-language storefronts ("COPIAS", "PROMOCION"), the dot-as-thousands-separator price format (4.995), the hexagonal paving stones, the ornate gazebo, and the curved mid-century apartment block typical of the area around Plaza 24 de Septiembre. The overcast sky and flocks of pigeons match the central plaza microclimate.

