Left-hand traffic, the yellow diamond road sign, and the colonial wooden church point to New Zealand. The preserved steam locomotive beside a harbour backed by rolling hills is characteristic of Port Chalmers on the Otago Peninsula near Dunedin, with the water being Otago Harbour. The concrete wharf posts on the right confirm a historic port setting.

