This is a right-hand-drive European motorway (broken centre line, W-beam guardrails, German-style lattice transmission pylon) running through a broad flat valley flanked by low, rounded, partly forested hills with terraced slopes that read as vineyards. That combination of a wide rift-valley floor, temperate spruce-and-broadleaf woodland, and vineyard terracing points strongly to the Rhine/Mosel valley in western Germany rather than the higher Alps. The terrain and pylon design fit the Rhineland-Palatinate area around the A61/A60 corridor near Bingen.

